        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "503cebf6-c0e4-5297-af07-435e39291f70",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hugh Keays-Byrne, George Miller, Byron Kennedy, Mel Gibson, Joanne Samuel, Steve Bisley, Tim Burns, Roger Ward, Igor Auzins, Miles Buchanan, Simone Buchanan, Kate Fitzpatrick, Ron Haddrick\n- Works: Stone, Mad Max, Runaway Island, Farscape\n- Roles: Toad, Toecutter, Immortan Joe, Grunchlk, Mad Max Rockatansky\n- Topics: Australian film, television film, science fiction television\n\nFacts:\n- In 1974, Hugh Keays-Byrne played Toad in the film Stone.\n- In 1979, Mad Max was released as an Australian dystopian action film directed by George Miller and produced by Byron Kennedy.\n- In 1979, Hugh Keays-Byrne played the main antagonist Toecutter in Mad Max.\n- In 1979, Mel Gibson starred in Mad Max as Mad Max Rockatansky, alongside Joanne Samuel, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Steve Bisley, Tim Burns, and Roger Ward.\n- In 1982, Runaway Island was released as an Australian television film directed by Igor Auzins.\n- In 1982, Runaway Island starred Miles Buchanan, Simone Buchanan, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Kate Fitzpatrick, and Ron Haddrick.\n- Hugh Keays-Byrne later played the main antagonist Immortan Joe in the 2015 film Mad Max: Fury Road.\n- Hugh Keays-Byrne also played Grunchlk in the science fiction television series Farscape.\n- Outside Australia, Hugh Keays-Byrne is best known for his roles in Stone, Mad Max, Mad Max: Fury Road, and Farscape.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f9d78d43-60bc-598e-85e5-60e06e23e897",
        "text": "Page: Hugh Keays-Byrne. Sentence: Outside Australia, he is best known for his role as \"Toad\" in the 1974 movie \"Stone\", the main antagonist \"Toecutter\" in the 1979 film \"Mad Max\", the main antagonist \"Immortan Joe\" in the 2015 film \"\", and \"Grunchlk\" in the science fiction television series \"Farscape\".\nPage: Mad Max. Sentence: Mad Max is a 1979 Australian dystopian action film directed by George Miller, produced by Byron Kennedy, and starring Mel Gibson as \"Mad\" Max Rockatansky, Joanne Samuel, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Steve Bisley, Tim Burns, and Roger Ward.\nPage: Runaway Island (1982 film). Sentence: Runaway Island is a 1982 Australian television film directed by Igor Auzins and starring Miles Buchanan, Simone Buchanan, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Kate Fitzpatrick, and Ron Haddrick.",
